  "description": "A parametric TV on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nSIZED BY DIAGONAL, which is the only dimension anyone knows about a television. A 16:9 panel is 0.871 × its diagonal wide and 0.490 tall, so width and height are DERIVED and the published \"Diagonal (inches)\" converts back — type 1.39 m and it reads 55\", which is the number on the box.\n\nSEGMENT-HOSTED, because most televisions are on a wall now. Drop it on one and it takes the wall's line; the plan is a thin sliver at the wall face, which is all a TV really occupies. Switch the mount to Stand and it grows a neck and a foot that project into the room — those are the only pieces that touch the floor, and they are the ones a plan needs.\n\nVIEWING DISTANCE at 1.6 × the diagonal is published for the same reason the TV unit publishes it: it is where the sofa goes, and it is the one measurement that connects this object to the room around it.",
